.TH PKGDEL 1 "2026-09-07" "emerald" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pkgdel \- remove an installed Emerald package
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkgdel
.RI [ options ]
.I portname
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pkgdel
removes the named installed package and updates the package database. Removing a package may affect dependents; use Emerald dependency commands before removal. Root privileges are required unless operating in an explicitly permitted custom root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help.
.TP
.B -v, --verbose
Print removed files.
.TP
.B --root=PATH
Remove from PATH instead of the system root.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success; non-zero if the package is absent, protected, or removal fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkgadd (1),
.BR pkgbase (1),
.BR emerald (1)
